For $i < \mu$ let $B_i$ hold the earlier cliques and all their non-neighbors. A vertex of $C_j$ has fewer than $
u_j$ non-neighbors, so $|B_i| < \kappa$ as $i < \operatorname{cf} \kappa$. Pick $
u_i$ with $|X^{
u_i}| > |B_i|$ and $|X^{
u_i}| \ge \kappa_i$, for cardinals $\kappa_i$ cofinal in $\kappa$. By induction on $\kappa$, $X^{
u_i} \setminus B_i$ holds a clique $C_i$ of size $|X^{
u_i}|$.
